# Wave W17-V (Route 206): pillar pine — a shadow pine in cool deep greens, tiered and full, grown straight and dark in the cycleway’s shade with its highlight lifted clear of the turf, on pillar turf (ground baked in). Route 206’s own tree — split from Route 205’s wind-bent gale pine by posture entire (shade-straight vs wind-bent) and from Route 203’s dusted coal pine by the clean cool crown (pillar shade vs mine smoke).
